  "judgment": [
    "Matched outcomes remain close in aggregate: solo +16 wins (one failed baseline excluded), two troops -4, four troops unchanged, six troops +3. Retain all 116 adverse reversals; aggregate similarity does not negate individual deaths.",
    "Mixed parties and all three six-pet family rotations do not universally exceed six troops. Mean hero damage share remains approximately 62\u201371% in these party configurations; the hero still contributes most actual damage. These observations do not establish a universal optimal roster.",
    "All eleven pet families used both kits and experienced actual interruptions; support/ward output and survival differ. No recorded permanent immunity appears in the family summaries. This complements the dedicated pet behavior regressions, rather than replacing them.",
    "The worst matched 20-case strata lose four wins: trained Normal Highlands Paladin/four troops and low-investment Nightmare Frontier Mage/two troops. These are small deterministic strata, not estimated player win probabilities; no broad numeric retune follows from them.",
    "Of the 116 lost baseline wins, 106 end in hero death and 10 are living timeouts. Three suspicious timeout configurations were replayed solely with an observational subclass for diagnosis; these do not replace or augment the original 6,912 result set.",
    "Crown trained Nightmare Paladin/six troops: the scripted policy repeatedly orders attacks against a returning native Ashbeast while the hero stays at full health. This exposes the scripted targeting policy/encounter-reset interaction and cannot be interpreted as a pure damage deficit. The original timeout is retained.",
    "Frontier low Nightmare Ranger/solo: native encounter population adds a captain during the observation; targets move and HP changes through the time cap. Highlands low Normal Ranger/six troops: Ridge continues authored attack/retreat/healing phases with five troops alive. These traces show ongoing encounters rather than a universal motion/cast deadlock.",
    "The fixed observation policy, two seeds, artificial encounter setups, six-unit cap-stress rows and 90-second cap constrain inference. No human playability, physical-device comfort or listening certification is claimed."
  ],
  "releaseDisposition": "Balance review supports retaining current tuning. Release remains blocked by final exact-source hosted browser/game gates and publication approval; do not claim merged or ready solely from this review."
}
